@* Light/dark switch. The persisted theme is applied before first paint by the
   inline script in App.razor; this component only offers the toggle.

   Plain JS rather than an @onclick, and both icons rendered with CSS picking one rather than a
   field deciding: the login page renders statically (see App.razor's render-mode gate), where
   there is no circuit to dispatch an event to and no JS interop to ask the current theme with.
   The same change means the switch also works on every other page before the circuit has
   finished connecting, rather than sitting dead for a moment with the wrong icon. *@

<button type="button"
        class="fh-theme-toggle"
        title="@UiText.Components.ToggleTheme"
        aria-label="@UiText.Components.ToggleTheme"
        onclick="themeInterop.toggle()">
	<i class="bi bi-moon-stars fh-theme-toggle__in-light" aria-hidden="true"></i>
	<i class="bi bi-sun fh-theme-toggle__in-dark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
</button>
